<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- RUST_CATHEDRAL_MECHANICS_1 §2, Tier 3 — the sacred tier. NOT a
       mineable (no <mineable>, no building.isResourceRock/mineableThing):
       this is a plain faction-owned BUILDING, ParentName="BuildingBase"
       (vanilla Wall's own parent, read via mcp__rimsage__get_def_details),
       not RockBase — the spec is explicit these are buildings, not rock.

       Faction ownership is NOT a ThingDef field (RimWorld sets faction on
       the spawned Thing instance, not the def) — it is applied by
       Source/GenStep_ScatterSacredWalls.cs at placement time, calling
       `.SetFaction(Faction.OfMechanoids)`. Faction defName confirmed
       against the live/vendor def: vanilla `Mechanoid` (hidden,
       permanentEnemy) is the faction the_rust_cathedral.md's "faction 13"
       already reskins to "the Forgotten Arsenal" / "the Forsaken Arsenal"
       (src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Patches/ForgottenArsenal.xml, label +
       description only, no new FactionDef) — this def and its genstep
       reuse that SAME faction rather than inventing a second one.

       Destroying or claiming a faction-owned building fires vanilla's own
       AttackedBuilding goodwill hook automatically — engine-default on any
       faction-owned Thing, confirmed by the item brief, no new code needed
       for that half. The −15 magnitude and the hum-irritation bump both
       ride §1 (the hum-mood system, NOT YET BUILT) — noted here, not
       stubbed: no numeric hook, no MapComponent reference, nothing this
       file can silently get wrong before §1 exists.

       v1 SCOPE (kit spec, "one sacred wall variant"): this is the one
       variant. "Rarer, stranger wall types" are explicitly deferred to a
       content pass, same as the ~10-building sacred-tier roster overall.

       Not deconstructible/mineable and not player-buildable
       (designationCategory omitted) — this exists only where
       GenStep_ScatterSacredWalls places it; a player cannot construct a
       second one.

       PLACEHOLDER ART: RockFlecked_Atlas again (Graphic_Single — safe for
       an isolated, non-linked placement, same choice MineableSteel itself
       makes), tinted toward verdigris/gold to read as ornamented rather
       than raw wall. Real bespoke sacred-wall art is owed (art pipe). -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="BuildingBase">
    <defName>RUT_SacredWall_Conduit</defName>
    <thingClass>Building</thingClass>
    <label>sacred conduit wall</label>
    <description>A run of wall unlike the plate around it — patterned, deliberate, untouched by the drift that banks against everything else here. Nothing about it explains itself. Only that it is watched, and that touching it is a choice.</description>
    <category>Building</category>
    <altitudeLayer>Building</altitudeLayer>
    <passability>Impassable</passability>
    <fillPercent>1</fillPercent>
    <coversFloor>true</coversFloor>
    <blockLight>true</blockLight>
    <blockWind>true</blockWind>
    <holdsRoof>true</holdsRoof>
    <neverMultiSelect>true</neverMultiSelect>
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <mineable>false</mineable>
    <leaveResourcesWhenKilled>false</leaveResourcesWhenKilled>
    <tickerType>Never</tickerType>
    <staticSunShadowHeight>1</staticSunShadowHeight>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/Linked/RockFlecked_Atlas</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
      <color>(196,168,74)</color>
      <colorTwo>(64,92,80)</colorTwo>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>2200</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <Beauty>2</Beauty>
    </statBases>
    <building>
      <isInert>true</isInert>
      <deconstructible>false</deconstructible>
    </building>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
